{"format":1,"key":"zone:westernplaguelands","path":"/lore/zone/westernplaguelands","name":"Western Plaguelands","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"westernplaguelands","name":"Western Plaguelands","path":"/lore/zone/westernplaguelands"},"levels":"","description":"Once the fertile agricultural breadbasket of northern Lordaeron, the Western Plaguelands now choke beneath a toxic mist and legions of undead. While…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:westernplaguelands","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Once the fertile agricultural breadbasket of northern Lordaeron, the Western Plaguelands now choke beneath a toxic mist and legions of undead. While Kel'Thuzad's cauldrons ruined the region's farms and towns, the soil still clings tenaciously to life. The Argent Dawn, the Alliance, the Forsaken, and the Scarlet Crusade all wage desperate campaigns across its blighted fields.","Before the Third War, this land was a verdant corridor of farms stretching east from Tirisfal Glades toward Darrowmere Lake. Hearthglen governed the northern administration from Mardenholde Keep, while the sprawling town of Andorhal orchestrated the storage and export of grain across the kingdom. That crucial agricultural role made the region Kel'Thuzad's primary target. By introducing the Plague of Undeath directly into the grain shipments at Andorhal, the Cult of the Damned turned Lordaeron's sustenance into its doom.","To permanently poison the soil, the Scourge raised four massive plague cauldrons across the largest agricultural estates: Felstone Field, Dalson's Tears, the Writhing Haunt, and Gahrron's Withering. Today, monstrous Cauldron Lords maintain these noxious vats, pumping venomous fog into the atmosphere. The surrounding trees twist with swollen, tumorous growths, and blighted wildlife rampages through the brush. Beneath Caer Darrow on Darrowmere Lake, Darkmaster Gandling trains necromancers within Scholomance, compounding the undead threat.","Despite the omnipresence of the Scourge, several factions maintain embattled footholds. The Scarlet Crusade controls the fortress of Hearthglen in the north, purging anything they deem tainted with rabid zeal. To the south, Alliance forces stage from Chillwind Camp, while the Forsaken defend their borders at the Bulwark. Mediating and directing the fight against the undead cauldrons is the neutral Argent Dawn, which aids champions of both factions and guards Uther's Tomb—the last truly sanctified ground in the region."],"hash":"dc8171","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"86be802e32","sec":119},"female-narrator":{"sha":"936d505e10","sec":122}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Western Plaguelands (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Western_Plaguelands_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Western Plaguelands","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Western_Plaguelands"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/zone/easternplaguelands","n":"Eastern Plaguelands","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/ruins-of-andorhal","n":"Ruins of Andorhal","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/scholomance","n":"Scholomance","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/hearthglen","n":"Hearthglen","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/uther-s-tomb","n":"Uther's Tomb","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/bulwark","n":"Bulwark","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/chillwind-camp","n":"Chillwind Camp","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/topic/scourge","n":"Scourge","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/zone/tirisfal","n":"Tirisfal Glades","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/chillwind-point","n":"Chillwind Point","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/strahnbrad","n":"Strahnbrad","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/quest/1791-the-windwatcher","n":"The Windwatcher","k":"quest"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/andorhal","n":"Andorhal","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/bulwark","n":"Bulwark","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/caer-darrow","n":"Caer Darrow","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/chillwind-camp","n":"Chillwind Camp","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dalson